            <fr:title text="Triton">Triton</fr:title>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>A Python-embedded <fr:link href="/5PSC/" title="Kernel DSLs" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/5PSC/" display-uri="5PSC" type="local">DSL</fr:link> for GPU kernels in which you write <html:em>block</html:em>-level code — load a tile, do arithmetic on it, store it — and the compiler decides how the tile maps onto threads <html:span class="link-reference"><fr:link href="/tilletTritonIntermediateLanguage2019/" title="Triton: An intermediate language and compiler for tiled neural network computations" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/tilletTritonIntermediateLanguage2019/" display-uri="tilletTritonIntermediateLanguage2019" type="local">[tilletTritonIntermediateLanguage2019]</fr:link></html:span>. That is the trade against CUDA: you give up control of the thread indexing that <fr:link href="/U1FO/" title="Memory coalescing merges a warp's accesses into one transaction per cache line" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/U1FO/" display-uri="U1FO" type="local">memory coalescing</fr:link> depends on, and in exchange you stop writing it.</html:p>
            <html:p>The compiler is built on <fr:link href="/IR7B/" title="MLIR" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/IR7B/" display-uri="IR7B" type="local">MLIR</fr:link>, with two custom dialects, and the boundary between them is the single most useful thing to know when a kernel is slow (<fr:link href="/9N7G/" title="The prefix says which side of layout assignment" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/9N7G/" display-uri="9N7G" type="local">The prefix says which side of layout assignment</fr:link>). <html:code>ttir</html:code> (<html:code>tt.</html:code> ops) is the target-independent tensor level — roughly what you wrote. <html:code>ttgir</html:code> (<html:code>ttg.</html:code> ops) is after layout assignment, where every tensor carries an <html:em>encoding</html:em> saying which lane holds which element (<fr:link href="/RI0V/" title="An encoding tiles the block across threads and warps" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/RI0V/" display-uri="RI0V" type="local">An encoding tiles the block across threads and warps</fr:link>).</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>So a Triton performance problem is one of two things, and the dialect prefix tells you which.</html:strong> At the <html:code>tt.</html:code> level it is your algorithm — the tiling, the loop structure, the arithmetic. At the <html:code>ttg.</html:code> level it is the compiler's distribution of it, and the usual culprit is a <html:code>ttg.convert_layout</html:code> that round-trips a tensor through <fr:link href="/8GZN/" title="Shared memory (GPU)" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/8GZN/" display-uri="8GZN" type="local">shared memory</fr:link> inside a loop (<fr:link href="/B4XO/" title="A convert_layout round-trips through shared memory" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/B4XO/" display-uri="B4XO" type="local">A convert_layout round-trips through <fr:link href="/8GZN/" title="Shared memory (GPU)" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/8GZN/" display-uri="8GZN" type="local">shared memory</fr:link></fr:link>). The second kind is invisible in your source and obvious in the IR, which is the argument for reading the IR.</html:p>
            <html:p>From XLA's side a Triton kernel is an opaque <html:code>@triton_kernel_call</html:code> custom call (<fr:link href="/M18X/" title="XLA custom call" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/M18X/" display-uri="M18X" type="local">XLA custom call</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/2MM7/" title="A custom call is a black box XLA cannot fuse across" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/2MM7/" display-uri="2MM7" type="local">A <fr:link href="/M18X/" title="XLA custom call" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/M18X/" display-uri="M18X" type="local">custom call</fr:link> is a black box <fr:link href="/M74N/" title="XLA Compilation" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/M74N/" display-uri="M74N" type="local">XLA</fr:link> cannot fuse across</fr:link>), so nothing fuses across it — the same bargain <fr:link href="/060Z/" title="Pallas" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/060Z/" display-uri="060Z" type="local">Pallas</fr:link> makes on TPU.</html:p>
            <fr:tree show-metadata="false" toc="false">
              <fr:frontmatter>
                <fr:authors>
