                <fr:route>/RI0V/</fr:route>
                <fr:title text="An encoding tiles the block across threads and warps">An encoding tiles the block across threads and warps</fr:title>
                <fr:taxon>Card</fr:taxon>
                <fr:meta name="anki">1787404869920</fr:meta>
                <fr:meta name="anki-deck">MLSys</fr:meta>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
  <html:p>Read <html:code><![CDATA[tensor<128x64xf16, #blocked>]]></html:code> where <html:code><![CDATA[#blocked = #ttg.blocked<{sizePerThread=[1,4], threadsPerWarp=[8,4], warpsPerCTA=[4,1], order=[1,0]}>]]></html:code></html:p>
  
  
  
 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(63, 83, 127);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(63, 83, 127);" /> 
  <html:details><html:summary><html:span class="foldout" style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);">Answer</html:span></html:summary>
  The encoding says how the logical <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[128 \times  64]]></fr:tex> tile is distributed:

  <html:ul><html:li><html:strong><html:code>sizePerThread</html:code></html:strong> — elements each thread holds per dimension; the minor-dimension entry is the vectorisation width.</html:li>
    <html:li><html:strong><html:code>threadsPerWarp</html:code></html:strong> — how the 32 lanes of a <fr:link href="/OGCS5/" title="Warp (GPU)" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/OGCS5/" display-uri="OGCS5" type="local">Warp (GPU)</fr:link> are arranged in two dimensions.</html:li>
    <html:li><html:strong><html:code>warpsPerCTA</html:code></html:strong> — how warps tile the block.</html:li>
    <html:li><html:strong><html:code>order</html:code></html:strong> — minor-to-major, so which dimension is contiguous per thread (<fr:link href="/RR6G/" title="The layout is minor-to-major" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/RR6G/" display-uri="RR6G" type="local">The layout is minor-to-major</fr:link>).</html:li></html:ul>

  <html:strong>Multiply the three lists out and you get the tile one CTA covers in one pass</html:strong>: <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[1 \times  8 \times  4 = 32]]></fr:tex> rows and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[4 \times  4 \times  1 = 16]]></fr:tex> columns here, so the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[128 \times  64]]></fr:tex> shape takes <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[4 \times  4]]></fr:tex> repeats. That arithmetic is the whole content of the attribute, and it is how you check by hand whether loads coalesce.
</html:details>
</html:div>



</fr:mainmatter>
            </fr:tree>
            <fr:tree show-metadata="false" toc="false">
              <fr:frontmatter>
                <fr:authors>
                  <fr:author>
                    <fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link>
                  </fr:author>
