                <fr:uri>https://kellenkanarios.com/B4XO/</fr:uri>
                <fr:display-uri>B4XO</fr:display-uri>
                <fr:route>/B4XO/</fr:route>
                <fr:title text="A convert_layout round-trips through shared memory">A convert_layout round-trips through <fr:link href="/8GZN/" title="Shared memory (GPU)" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/8GZN/" display-uri="8GZN" type="local">shared memory</fr:link></fr:title>
                <fr:taxon>Card</fr:taxon>
                <fr:meta name="anki">1787404867395</fr:meta>
                <fr:meta name="anki-deck">MLSys</fr:meta>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
  <html:p>Why is <html:code>ttg.convert_layout</html:code> the op to look for in a slow <fr:link href="/CQ6W/" title="Triton" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/CQ6W/" display-uri="CQ6W" type="local">Triton</fr:link> kernel?</html:p>
  
  
  
 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(63, 83, 127);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(63, 83, 127);" /> 
  <html:details><html:summary><html:span class="foldout" style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);">Answer</html:span></html:summary>
  It re-distributes a tensor from one encoding to another (<fr:link href="/RI0V/" title="An encoding tiles the block across threads and warps" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/RI0V/" display-uri="RI0V" type="local">An encoding tiles the block across threads and warps</fr:link>) — typically <html:code><![CDATA[#blocked]]></html:code> to a <html:code><![CDATA[#ttg.dot_op]]></html:code> or <html:code><![CDATA[#mma]]></html:code> operand layout, because the tensor core wants its operands arranged differently from the way the loads produced them.

  <html:strong>Unless the conversion happens to be a pure register permutation, it round-trips through <fr:link href="/8GZN/" title="Shared memory (GPU)" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/8GZN/" display-uri="8GZN" type="local">shared memory</fr:link> and inserts barriers.</html:strong> That is a store, a sync across the block, and a load — for data that never changed value.

  One unnecessary <html:code>convert_layout</html:code> inside a loop body is a classic Triton performance bug, and it is visible in the IR long before it is visible in a profile. The layout-propagation passes exist to hoist these out of loops or eliminate them, so one that survives in the body is worth understanding rather than accepting.
</html:details>
</html:div>



</fr:mainmatter>
            </fr:tree>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors>
              <fr:author>
                <fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link>
              </fr:author>
            </fr:authors>
            <fr:date>
              <fr:year>2026</fr:year>
              <fr:month>8</fr:month>
              <fr:day>22</fr:day>
            </fr:date>
            <fr:uri>https://kellenkanarios.com/2MM7/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>2MM7</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/2MM7/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="A custom call is a black box XLA cannot fuse across">A <fr:link href="/M18X/" title="XLA custom call" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/M18X/" display-uri="M18X" type="local">custom call</fr:link> is a black box <fr:link href="/M74N/" title="XLA Compilation" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/M74N/" display-uri="M74N" type="local">XLA</fr:link> cannot fuse across</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Card</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="anki">1787404866279</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="anki-deck">MLSys</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
  <html:p>Read <html:code><![CDATA[custom-call(%a, %b), custom_call_target="tpu_custom_call", operand_layout_constraints={...}, backend_config="...", api_version=API_VERSION_STATUS_RETURNING]]></html:code></html:p>
  
  
  
 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(63, 83, 127);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(63, 83, 127);" /> 
  <html:details><html:summary><html:span class="foldout" style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);">Answer</html:span></html:summary>
  The escape hatch to code XLA does not generate: library kernels (cuBLAS, cuDNN), <fr:link href="/060Z/" title="Pallas" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/060Z/" display-uri="060Z" type="local">Pallas</fr:link> and <fr:link href="/M3MH/" title="Mosaic" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/M3MH/" display-uri="M3MH" type="local">Mosaic</fr:link> or <fr:link href="/CQ6W/" title="Triton" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/CQ6W/" display-uri="CQ6W" type="local">Triton</fr:link> kernels (<fr:link href="/QRDW/" title="A Pallas kernel is an opaque custom call" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/QRDW/" display-uri="QRDW" type="local">A <fr:link href="/060Z/" title="Pallas" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/060Z/" display-uri="060Z" type="local">Pallas</fr:link> kernel is an opaque <fr:link href="/M18X/" title="XLA custom call" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/M18X/" display-uri="M18X" type="local">custom call</fr:link></fr:link>), host callbacks.

  <html:ul><html:li><html:code>custom_call_target</html:code> selects the registered handler by name.</html:li>
    <html:li><html:code>backend_config</html:code> carries the opaque payload — a serialised Mosaic module, a tuning configuration, an algorithm choice.</html:li>
    <html:li><html:code>operand_layout_constraints</html:code> pins the layouts the handler requires (<fr:link href="/RR6G/" title="The layout is minor-to-major" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/RR6G/" display-uri="RR6G" type="local">The layout is minor-to-major</fr:link>).</html:li></html:ul>

  <html:strong>Everything expensive about a custom call follows from XLA not being able to see inside it.</html:strong> It cannot fuse across the boundary, so the operands are materialised to <fr:link href="/AI2G/" title="High bandwidth memory" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/AI2G/" display-uri="AI2G" type="local">High bandwidth memory</fr:link> and the results read back; it must assume the declared effects, so it cannot reorder freely; and the pinned layouts can force <html:code>copy</html:code> ops on both sides (<fr:link href="/KG5S/" title="bitcast is free, copy is not" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/KG5S/" display-uri="KG5S" type="local">bitcast is free, copy is not</fr:link>).

  A hand-written kernel has to beat all of that, not just the kernel XLA would have emitted.
</html:details>
</html:div>



</fr:mainmatter>
