            <fr:title text="A Pallas kernel is an opaque custom call">A <fr:link href="/060Z/" title="Pallas" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/060Z/" display-uri="060Z" type="local">Pallas</fr:link> kernel is an opaque <fr:link href="/M18X/" title="XLA custom call" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/M18X/" display-uri="M18X" type="local">custom call</fr:link></fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Card</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="anki">1787404869695</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="anki-deck">MLSys</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
  <html:p>How does a <fr:link href="/060Z/" title="Pallas" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/060Z/" display-uri="060Z" type="local">Pallas</fr:link> or <fr:link href="/CQ6W/" title="Triton" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/CQ6W/" display-uri="CQ6W" type="local">Triton</fr:link> kernel appear in a <fr:link href="/84N5/" title="StableHLO" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/84N5/" display-uri="84N5" type="local">StableHLO</fr:link> dump?</html:p>
  
  
  
 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(63, 83, 127);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(63, 83, 127);" /> 
  <html:details><html:summary><html:span class="foldout" style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);">Answer</html:span></html:summary>
  As an opaque custom call (<fr:link href="/M18X/" title="XLA custom call" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/M18X/" display-uri="M18X" type="local">XLA custom call</fr:link>):

  <html:pre><html:code class="language-llvm"><![CDATA[stablehlo.custom_call @tpu_custom_call(%a, %b) {backend_config = "...", api_version = 2 : i32}
  : (tensor<8x128xf32>, ...) -> tensor<8x128xf32>]]></html:code></html:pre>

  On GPU the target is <html:code>@triton_kernel_call</html:code> instead.

  <html:strong>The kernel body is not in this IR.</html:strong> It is serialised inside <html:code>backend_config</html:code> — a <fr:link href="/M3MH/" title="Mosaic" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/M3MH/" display-uri="M3MH" type="local">Mosaic</fr:link> module, or Triton IR (<fr:link href="/9N7G/" title="The prefix says which side of layout assignment" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/9N7G/" display-uri="9N7G" type="local">The prefix says which side of layout assignment</fr:link>) — and XLA treats the whole thing as a black box with declared operands, results, and effects.

  That is the trade you accept when you write a kernel by hand: you get control of the inner loop, and you give up every cross-op optimisation at the boundary, because the compiler cannot fuse across something it cannot see (<fr:link href="/2MM7/" title="A custom call is a black box XLA cannot fuse across" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/2MM7/" display-uri="2MM7" type="local">A <fr:link href="/M18X/" title="XLA custom call" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/M18X/" display-uri="M18X" type="local">custom call</fr:link> is a black box <fr:link href="/M74N/" title="XLA Compilation" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/M74N/" display-uri="M74N" type="local">XLA</fr:link> cannot fuse across</fr:link>).
</html:details>
</html:div>



